Clock Master ⏰
A Python-based, console-driven time management system built inside a Jupyter Notebook (Clock_Master_Project.ipynb). This project provides essential time-tracking utilities with clean terminal interfaces and interactive keyboard controls.

🚀 Features
Digital Clock

Displays a live, real-time digital clock showing the current date and time (DD-MM-YYYY HH:MM:SS).

Updates every second.

Alarm Clock

Allows users to set a custom alarm in HH:MM:SS format with input validation.

Continuously monitors the current time and triggers an audio alert (\a) along with a notification message when the alarm time is reached.

Stopwatch

Accurately tracks elapsed time in HH:MM:SS format.

Smoothly updates on the console using dynamic carriage returns (\r).

Countdown Timer

Accepts custom countdown durations (HH:MM:SS).

Counts down second-by-second with a visual timer display and alerts when time runs out.

Interactive Main Menu

An easy-to-navigate command-line interface that allows users to switch between tools or exit gracefully.

Includes robust exception handling (KeyboardInterrupt support via Ctrl+C and invalid input handling).

🛠️ Built With
Python (Core Logic)

datetime module (For real-time tracking and formatting)

time module (For delays and loops)
